# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Student data. None of this is ever committed.
#
# A transcription IS the student's answer; a cover strip IS their
# marks. The handoff carries 50 real students' scripts and the gold
# set carries what a faculty member awarded them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
handoff/
gold/covers/

# gold/gold_marks.csv is deliberately NOT ignored, and it is the only
# student-derived file that is not. It holds booklet ids and numbers -
# no name, no USN, no handwriting - while the crops it was read from,
# which show both, are ignored above. It is also the one artifact here
# that cannot be regenerated by running anything: it was read by eye,
# once. Losing it to a cautious gitignore would cost more than
# versioning a table of pseudonymous integers.

# ALL of output/, not just the obvious parts. Anything this project
# writes about a booklet quotes the student to justify itself - the
# alignment proposals carry answer excerpts, the marks carry the
# evidence quote a tier awarded on, the review queues carry both. An
# allowlist here would be one new output file away from leaking.
output/

# The schemes themselves are the department's, not ours to publish.
keys/scheme_pages/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
